---
export const prerender = true;
import Layout from '~/layouts/Layout.astro';
import ContentSection from '~/components/sections/ContentSection.astro';
import FeaturesList from '~/components/sections/FeaturesList.astro';
import FeatureItem from '~/components/ui/FeatureItem.astro';
import PageHeader from '~/components/layout/PageHeader.astro';
import Section from '~/components/layout/Section.astro';
import Container from '~/components/ui/Container.astro';
import Heading from '~/components/ui/Heading.astro';
import Text from '~/components/ui/Text.astro';
import Button from '~/components/ui/Button.astro';
import { Database, Layers, Users, Shield, Code, Server } from 'lucide-react';
import { ACTION_LINKS } from '~/site.config';
import Tbd from '~/components/common/Tbd.astro';

// Every claim here is also made in src/data/llms-intro.md and on the home
// page. Keep them in step: this page is what llms.txt calls "why Semantius exists".
const principles = [
    { title: 'Your Data Stays Yours', description: 'Every entity you define is a real PostgreSQL table. You can query it, back it up and take it with you.', icon: Database },
    { title: 'One Model, Four Surfaces', description: 'The same model drives the database, the REST API, the UI people work in and the tools agents call. There is no second schema to keep in sync.', icon: Layers },
    { title: 'People and Agents Together', description: 'People get dashboards, forms and grids generated from the model. AI chats and coding agents connect through MCP servers and a CLI.', icon: Users },
    { title: 'Guardrails by Default', description: 'An agent acts under the same permissions, validation rules and row level rules as any person. Granting access never means handing over unrestricted SQL.', icon: Shield },
    { title: 'Open Source', description: 'The core, the web app, the identity provider and the self-hosted stack are all released under the MIT license.', icon: Code },
    { title: 'Run It Your Way', description: 'Self-host the whole stack for free, run the core on managed Postgres such as Neon or Supabase, or let the managed cloud operate it.', icon: Server },
];
---

<Layout title="About - Semantius Agentic Data Platform" description="Why Semantius exists: one semantic model, owned by you, that serves your team and your agents from a PostgreSQL database you control.">
<PageHeader title='Why <span class="text-primary">Semantius</span> Exists' description='One semantic model, owned by you, that serves your team and your agents from a PostgreSQL database you control.' />

  {/* The paragraph from the founder's v1 specification, §4.11. */}
  <Section class="py-8!">
      <Container class="max-w-3xl">
          <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed">Semantius is a product of adenin Technologies, building business software since 1999. Everything you run yourself is MIT-licensed, so your system keeps working whatever happens.</p>
          <Tbd class="mt-3" note="Add this paragraph to the page, or replace the page with it?" />
      </Container>
  </Section>

  <ContentSection title='The Third Option'>
    <Text>Business data now has two kinds of readers: the people who run the business and the AI agents that act for them. Until now, a team that needed both had two choices.</Text>
    <Text>It could buy a SaaS product and bend the business to fit it, with the data locked inside. Or it could build something custom and maintain that code forever.</Text>
    <Text>Semantius is the third option. You describe your domain once as a semantic model: the entities, fields, relationships, roles and permissions. The database, the API, the UI and the guardrails for agents all follow from that model, and change when it changes.</Text>
  </ContentSection>

  <Section>
      <Container>
          <Heading level={2} class="text-center mb-12">What Semantius Stands For</Heading>
          <FeaturesList>
             {principles.map((p) => (
                 <FeatureItem title={p.title} description={p.description}>
                     <p.icon slot="icon" className="w-6 h-6" />
                 </FeatureItem>
             ))}
          </FeaturesList>
      </Container>
  </Section>

  <ContentSection title='Who Builds It'>
    <Text>Semantius is built by adenin. The source is developed in the open on <a href={ACTION_LINKS.social.github} class="text-primary hover:underline">GitHub</a>, where you can read the code and follow every release.</Text>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 pt-4">
      <Button href="/docs/overview">Get Started</Button>
      <Button href="/blueprints" variant="outline">Explore Blueprints</Button>
    </div>
  </ContentSection>
</Layout>
